{"t": 1792880372681, "cmd": "note", "args": ["--shot", "your_news_too_broad", "Full chronicle (Y), default 'Your news' view lists 100 of 137 entries at tick ~12000 (73%): other nations' rivalries, alliances and raids (e.g. 'Raiders from Westburg struck Northernland', 'Castleton and Blueton have become rivals') fill it. With ~20 NPC nations founded in day 1, 'neighbours' is almost everyone, so my 16 own entries (yellow, *) are scattered among 84 others. Expected 'Your news' to be noticeably narrower than All nations."]}
{"t": 1792880372897, "cmd": "note", "args": ["--shot", "only_my_nation_good", "'Only my nation' checkbox narrows to 16 of 137 entries, all mine, all highlighted yellow with * - this is the view that actually makes my news easy to find, but it is off by default and is a separate control from the Your news / All nations switch (two filters stacked; meaning of combo not obvious)."]}
